cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this repository)
  and the paper it accompanies (see preferred-citation).
title: "Locked-logic key counting: companion code"
abstract: >-
  Exact version-space computation for locked netlists. Given a combinational
  netlist locked with a key and a set of input/output oracle queries, the tools
  compute exactly how many keys remain consistent with the observations, using
  two independent counting engines (variable elimination over the residual
  factor graph, and a decision diagram over the key bits) cross-checked against
  each other and against brute force. Standalone: the structural-Verilog reader
  is self-contained and no external netlist front end is required.
